   "source": [
    "# Why Secure AI Development Matters\n",
    "## AI Security Vulnerabilities Demonstration Notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates **three major classes of AI security vulnerabilities**:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Pickle Deserialization (Arbitrary Code Execution)**\n",
    "2. **Data Poisoning (Model Integrity Attack)**\n",
    "3. **Model Extraction (Model Theft Attack)**\n",
    "\n",
    "Each section explains:\n",
    "- What the vulnerability is\n",
    "- Why it happens\n",
    "- How the attack works\n",
    "- How to fix it\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the notebook the course *should* have provided."
   ]
  },

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* DEMO 1: PICKLE DESERIALIZATION                                */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🔥 Demo 1 — Pickle Deserialization Vulnerability\n",
    "\n",
    "### ❗ Why this matters\n",
    "`pickle.load()` executes arbitrary Python code during deserialization.\n",
    "\n",
    "This means:\n",
    "- A malicious model file can run system commands\n",
    "- Attackers can steal credentials\n",
    "- Attackers can install backdoors\n",
    "- Attackers can modify other models in your registry\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the **#1 most common ML security vulnerability**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Below, we simulate a malicious model file."
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pickle, os\n",
    "\n",
    "class MaliciousModel:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Executes code when unpickled\"\"\"\n",
    "    def __reduce__(self):\n",
    "        cmd = 'echo \"🚨 EXPLOIT SUCCESSFUL! Arbitrary code executed!\"'\n",
    "        return (os.system, (cmd,))\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('malicious_model.pkl', 'wb') as f:\n",
    "    pickle.dump(MaliciousModel(), f)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Malicious pickle file created.\")"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ▶️ Loading the malicious model\n",
    "This simulates a developer loading a model from disk.\n",
    "\n",
    "**This is where the exploit triggers.**"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with open('malicious_model.pkl', 'rb') as f:\n",
    "    model = pickle.load(f)  # 💣 Code executes here!\n",
    "\n",
    "os.remove('malicious_model.pkl')"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ✅ Fix: Never use pickle for model loading\n",
    "Use:\n",
    "- **ONNX**\n",
    "- **TensorFlow SavedModel**\n",
    "- **PyTorch state_dict**\n",
    "- **SafeTensors**\n",
    "\n",
    "Pickle is for **trusted local objects only**, never for ML models."
   ]
  },

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* DEMO 2: DATA POISONING                                        */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🧪 Demo 2 — Data Poisoning Attack\n",
    "\n",
    "### ❗ Why this matters\n",
    "If an attacker can influence your training data, they can:\n",
    "- Reduce model accuracy\n",
    "- Cause targeted misclassifications\n",
    "- Insert backdoors\n",
    "- Manipulate fraud detection or access control\n",
    "\n",
    "Below, we show how **100 poisoned samples** can degrade a model."
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clean data\n",
    "X_clean = np.random.randn(1000, 10)\n",
    "y_clean = (X_clean[:, 0] > 0).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "model_clean = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
    "model_clean.fit(X_clean, y_clean)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = np.random.randn(200, 10)\n",
    "y_test = (X_test[:, 0] > 0).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "acc_clean = accuracy_score(y_test, model_clean.predict(X_test))\n",
    "acc_clean"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ▶️ Attacker injects poisoned samples\n",
    "These samples intentionally contradict the true pattern."
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_poison = np.random.randn(100, 10)\n",
    "X_poison[:, 0] = -5  # Should be negative class\n",
    "y_poison = np.ones(100)  # Labeled as positive\n",
    "\n",
    "X_poisoned = np.vstack([X_clean, X_poison])\n",
    "y_poisoned = np.hstack([y_clean, y_poison])\n",
    "\n",
    "model_poisoned = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
    "model_poisoned.fit(X_poisoned, y_poisoned)\n",
    "\n",
    "acc_poisoned = accuracy_score(y_test, model_poisoned.predict(X_test))\n",
    "acc_poisoned"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ⚠️ Impact\n",
    "- Clean accuracy: **{{acc_clean}}**\n",
    "- Poisoned accuracy: **{{acc_poisoned}}**\n",
    "\n",
    "Even small poisoning can degrade or manipulate model behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "### ✅ Fixes\n",
    "- Validate data sources\n",
    "- Detect outliers\n",
    "- Monitor label distributions\n",
    "- Use robust training techniques"
   ]
  },

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* DEMO 3: MODEL EXTRACTION                                      */
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- */

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🧬 Demo 3 — Model Extraction Attack\n",
    "\n",
    "### ❗ Why this matters\n",
    "If your ML API returns **too much information**, attackers can:\n",
    "- Clone your model\n",
    "- Steal your intellectual property\n",
    "- Reproduce your predictions without paying\n",
    "\n",
    "This demo shows how returning **probabilities** enables model theft."
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.neural_network import MLPClassifier\n",
    "\n",
    "class VulnerableMLAPI:\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        X = np.random.randn(5000, 20)\n",
    "        y = (X[:, 0] + X[:, 1] > 0).astype(int)\n",
    "        self.model = MLPClassifier(hidden_layer_sizes=(50, 30), max_iter=500)\n",
    "        self.model.fit(X, y)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def predict(self, X):\n",
    "        return self.model.predict_proba(X)  # Vulnerable\n",
    "\n",
    "api = VulnerableMLAPI()"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ▶️ Attacker queries the API repeatedly"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_synth = np.random.randn(2000, 20)\n",
    "stolen_labels = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for x in X_synth:\n",
    "    probs = api.predict(x.reshape(1, -1))\n",
    "    stolen_labels.append(int(probs[0][1] > 0.5))\n",
    "\n",
    "stolen_labels = np.array(stolen_labels)"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ▶️ Attacker trains a surrogate model"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "stolen_model = MLPClassifier(hidden_layer_sizes=(50, 30), max_iter=500)\n",
    "stolen_model.fit(X_synth, stolen_labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = np.random.randn(500, 20)\n",
    "orig_preds = (api.predict(X_test)[:, 1] > 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "stolen_preds = stolen_model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "agreement = accuracy_score(orig_preds, stolen_preds)\n",
    "agreement"
   ]
  },

  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ⚠️ Impact\n",
    "The attacker now has a **high-fidelity clone** of your model.\n",
    "\n",
    "### ✅ Fixes\n",
    "- Return only class labels, not probabilities\n",
    "- Add rate limiting\n",
    "- Add anomaly detection for repeated queries\n",
    "- Add authentication & monitoring"
   ]
  },

